==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|firezzan}}, {{m|goh|frezzan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*fraetaną}}. Cognate with {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|fråse}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|fret}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=5|frisst|fraß|gefressen|past subjunctive=fräße}}

# {{label|de|intransitive|of an animal}} to [[eat]]; to [[feed]]
# {{label|de|intransitive|of a person|colloquial}} to [[stuff]] oneself; to [[gorge]] oneself; to [[eat]] like a pig
# {{label|de|transitive|of an animal}} to [[devour]]; to [[eat]] (something)
# {{label|de|transitive|of a person|colloquial}} to [[stuff]] oneself on (something); to [[gorge]] on (something)
# {{label|de|transitive|colloquial|figuratively}} to [[guzzle]] (e.g. gas); to [[burn]] through (e.g. money)
# {{label|de|colloquial|perfect only}} to [[despise]], to have a [[pet peeve]] against
#: {{ux|de|Den hab' ich ja ''gefressen''.|Oh god, I hate that person. (Literally: I have eaten him.)}}

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-strong|fress|fraß|gefressen|h||friss|fräß|a|a|||a}}

====Usage notes====
'''''Fressen''''' contrasts with the more refined {{m|de|essen||to eat}}.

